    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0585" n="1545" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1545"/>

                <head>No. 1051.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rives to Mr. Kloss.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 23,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, in reply to Colonel
                    Frey’s note of the 31st of January last, inclosing a note dated 13th of January,
                    addressed to the Secretary of State, by the President of the Swiss
                    Confederation, on the subject of placing under one management the international
                    bureau for the protection of industrial property and the bureau of literary and
                    artistic works, to say that it is understood by this Government that in charging
                    the Swiss Government with the administration of these bureaus, the details of
                    their organization and management within the terms of the convention and final
                    protocol were left entirely to the discretion of your Government.</p>
                <p>There is no doubt that this trust will be discharged with due regard to the
                    interests of all the members of the International Union, and since the President
                    and Chancellor of the Swiss Confederation in their communication of January 13
                    declare that the step in question has been taken with a view to economical
                    administration, this Government cordially approves it.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. L. Rives</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
